    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70d1dcf1_5cb2780a",
        "filename": "src/core/SkRRect.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 769,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T18:03:33Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I would have thought that this would cover both `(min + rad \u003c\u003d max) \u0026\u0026 (max - rad \u003e\u003d min)`. `min + rad` is the same as `minCoord + radiusFromMin` or `ptFromMin`. Since we know the two radii are \u003e\u003d 0, then `maxCoord - radiusFromMax` should be \u003c\u003d `maxCoord`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 769,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 769,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "6f559bafbed4c8323a899df4008aa073df4eccc6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3504d60d_b255250d",
        "filename": "src/core/SkRRect.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 769,
      "author": {
        "id": 4623515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T22:10:22Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The thing about checking the addition is that this fails when min \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c max and/or radiusFromMin \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c radiusFromMax (or vice versa). \n\nThe reasoning here is that the addition will \"eat\" the smaller values due to float precision. Such as `min + max` evaluating to `max`.\n\nTesting every radius and coord individually makes sure that the arithmetic works across all the operations tested in `are_radius_check_predicates_valid`\n\nAt least this is my understanding. Please let me know what you think\n\nIf we wanted to be extra conservative we could include both this check and the ones in `are_radius_check_predicates_valid`, but I wasn\u0027t sure if that was too much redundancy.\n\n\nI thought to remove it because,\n* if `are_radius_check_predicates_valid` assures that all the radii exist within the bounds individually\n* then `are_radii_predicates_valid` can assure that the sum of those radii also exists within the bounds",
      "parentUuid": "7df2acfa_adcad36a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 769,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 769,
        "endChar": 19
